  {
   "speaker": "priya",
   "text": "What does an optimizer want with a tree?",
   "visuals": []
  },
  {
   "speaker": "ravi",
   "text": "Passes ask it constantly. Does a definition dominate every use? Can code hoist out of a loop? Is this edge a loop?",
   "visuals": []
  },
  {
   "speaker": "ravi",
   "text": "And D is where B and C stop dominating: their dominance frontier. A phi node belongs there. Here is LLVM's, at O1.",
   "visuals": [
    {
     "do": "world.set",
     "world": "term.session",
     "cwd": "~/dom",
     "prompt": "{cwd} %",
     "title": "zsh: ~/dom"
    },
    {
     "do": "term.highlight",
     "off": true
    },
    {
     "do": "define",
     "term": "dominance frontier",
     "at": 0.3
    },
    {
     "do": "term.run",
     "cmd": "clang -S -emit-llvm -O1 d.c -o - | grep phi",
     "out": [
      "  %8 = phi i32 [ %4, %3 ], [ %6, %5 ]"
     ],
     "cps": 40,
     "at": 0.6
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "speaker": "priya",
   "text": "It takes the value from one() or from two(), by the edge it arrived on.",
